with 1.0.15):\nL164:     The notation for the Mellin transform was changed to ℳf\\left(z\\right) from ℳ(f;z).\nL165: See also:\nL166:     Annotations for cite41†§2.5(i) , cite33†§2.5 and cite17†Ch.2 L167: The sum in (cite77†2.5.6 ) is taken over all poles of {x}^{-z}ℳf\\left(1-z\\right)ℳh\\left(z\\right) in the strip d<\\mathrm{\\Re }z<c, and it provides the asymptotic expansion of I(x) for small values of x. Similarly, if ℳf\\left(1-z\\right) and ℳh\\left(z\\right) can be continued analytically to meromorphic functions in a right half-plane, and if the vertical line of integration can be translated to the right, then we obtain an asymptotic expansion for I(x) for large values of x.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLMF: §25.2 Definition and Expansions ‣ Riemann Zeta Function ‣ Chapter 25 Zeta and Related Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2)\nciteturn128view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2\",\"lineno\":100}); Total lines: 319\nL13: # §25.2 Definition and Expansions\nL14: \nL15: ⓘ\nL16: \nL17: Keywords:\nL18:     cite11†Riemann zeta function , cite12†analytic properties L19: Notes:\nL20:     See Apostol (cite13†1976 , Chapter 12) and Ivić (cite14†1985 , Section 1.1).\nL21: Referenced by:\nL22:     cite15†§20.10(i) , cite16†§20.9(iii) L23: Permalink:\nL24:     cite17†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2 L25: See also:\nL26:     Annotations for cite18†Ch.25 L27: ###### Contents\nL28: \nL29:   1. cite19†§25.2(i) Definition L30:   2. cite20†§25.2(ii) Other Infinite Series L31:   3. cite21†§25.2(iii) Representations by the Euler–Maclaurin Formula L32:   4. cite22†§25.2(iv) Infinite Products L33: ## §25.2(i) Definition\nL34: \nL35: ⓘ\nL36: \nL37: Keywords:\nL38:     cite11†Riemann zeta function , cite23†definition L39: Notes:\nL40:     See Apostol (cite13†1976 , Chapter 12), Ivić (cite14†1985 , Section 1.1) and Riemann (cite24†1859 , p. 136).\nL41: Referenced by:\nL42:     cite25†§2.10(i) , cite26†§26.12(iv) , cite27†§27.1 , cite28†§27.18 , cite29†§27.4 , cite30†§8.22(ii) L43: Permalink:\nL44:     cite31†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.i L45: See also:\nL46:     Annotations for cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L47: \nL48: When \\mathrm{\\Re }s>1,\nL49: 25.2.1  |  | \\zeta \\left(s\\right)=\\sum _{n=1}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}\\frac{1}{{n}^{s}}.  |\nL50: ⓘ\nL51: Defines:\nL52:     \\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function\nL53: Symbols:\nL54:     cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L55: Keywords:\nL56:     cite23†definition , cite35†infinite series L57: Sources:\nL58:     Apostol (cite13†1976 , Chapter 12); Riemann (cite24†1859 , p. 136)\nL59: A&S Ref:\nL60:     23.2.1\nL61: Referenced by:\nL62:     cite36†(25.11.2) , cite37†(25.2.2) , cite38†(25.2.4) , cite39†§25.2(ii) , cite40†Erratum (V1.0.17) for Equation (25.2.4) L63: Permalink:\nL64:     cite41†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E1 L65: Encodings:\nL66:     cite42†TeX , cite43†pMML , cite44†png L67: See also:\nL68:     Annotations for cite45†§25.2(i) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L69: Elsewhere \\zeta \\left(s\\right) is defined by analytic continuation. It is a meromorphic function whose only singularity in ℂ is a simple pole at s=1, with residue 1.\nL70: ## §25.2(ii) Other Infinite Series\nL71: \nL72: ⓘ\nL73: Keywords:\nL74:     cite46†Dirichlet series , cite11†Riemann zeta function , cite47†derivatives , cite48†series expansions L75: Notes:\nL76:     See Hardy (cite49†1912 , pp. 215–216) and Ivić (cite14†1985 , Section 1.1).\nL77: Referenced by:\nL78:     cite50†Erratum (V1.0.23) for Subsection 25.2(ii) Other Infinite Series L79: Permalink:\nL80:     cite51†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.ii L81: Addition (effective with 1.0.23):\nL82:     Immediately above (cite52†25.2.5 ), it is now mentioned that {\\gamma }_{n} defines the Stieltjes constants.\nL83: See also:\nL84:     Annotations for cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L85: 25.2.2  |  | \\zeta \\left(s\\right)=\\frac{1}{1-{2}^{-s}}\\sum _{n=0}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}\\frac{1}{{(2n+1)}^{s}},  |\nL86: \\mathrm{\\Re }s>1.\nL87: ⓘ\nL88: Symbols:\nL89:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L90: Keywords:\nL91:     cite35†infinite series L92: Proof sketch:\nL93:     Derivable from (cite53†25.2.1 ).\nL94: A&S Ref:\nL95:     23.2.20 (is the special case with integer values of s)\nL96: Referenced by:\nL97:     cite55†(25.11.11) L98: Permalink:\nL99:     cite56†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E2 L100: Encodings:\nL101:     cite57†TeX , cite58†pMML , cite59†png L102: See also:\nL103:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L104: 25.2.3  |  | \\zeta \\left(s\\right)=\\frac{1}{1-{2}^{1-s}}\\sum _{n=1}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}\\frac{{(-1)}^{n-1}}{{n}^{s}},  |\nL105: \\mathrm{\\Re }s>0.\nL106: ⓘ\nL107: Symbols:\nL108:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L109: Keywords:\nL110:     cite35†infinite series L111: Source:\nL112:     Apostol (cite13†1976 , (27), p. 292)\nL113: A&S Ref:\nL114:     23.2.19 (is the special case with integer values of s)\nL115: Referenced by:\nL116:     cite61†§25.11(x) L117: Permalink:\nL118:     cite62†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E3 L119: Encodings:\nL120:     cite63†TeX , cite64†pMML , cite65†png L121: See also:\nL122:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L123: 25.2.4  |  | \\zeta \\left(s\\right)=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\sum _{n=0}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}}{n!}{\\gamma }_{n}{(s-1)}^{n},  |\nL124: ⓘ\nL125: Symbols:\nL126:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite52†{\\gamma }_{n}: Stieltjes constants , cite66†!: factorial (as in n!) , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L127: Keywords:\nL128:     cite67†Laurent series , cite35†infinite series L129: Sources:\nL130:     Hardy (cite49†1912 , p. 216); mistakenly missing factor of {(-1)}^{n}/n!; Ivić (cite14†1985 , (1.11), p. 4)\nL131: A&S Ref:\nL132:     23.2.5 (with unnecessary constraint removed)\nL133: Referenced by:\nL134:     cite68†Erratum (V1.0.17) for Equation (25.2.4) , cite69†Erratum (V1.0.23) for Subsection 25.2(ii) Other Infinite Series L135: Permalink:\nL136:     cite70†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E4 L137: Encodings:\nL138:     cite71†TeX , cite72†pMML , cite73†png L139: Clarification (effective with 1.0.17):\nL140:     Originally this equation had the constraint \\mathrm{\\Re }s>0. This constraint is unnecessary because, as stated after (cite53†25.2.1 ), \\zeta \\left(s\\right) is meromorphic with a simple pole at s=1. Suggested 2017-12-05 by John Harper\nL141: See also:\nL142:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L143: where the Stieltjes constants {\\gamma }_{n} are defined via\nL144: \nL145: 25.2.5  |  | {\\gamma }_{n}=\\underset{m\\to \\mathrm{\\infty }}{lim}\\left(\\sum _{k=1}^{m}\\frac{{(\\mathrm{ln}k)}^{n}}{k}-\\frac{{(\\mathrm{ln}m)}^{n+1}}{n+1}\\right).  |\nL146: ⓘ\nL147: Defines:\nL148:     {\\gamma }_{n}: Stieltjes constants\nL149: Symbols:\nL150:     cite74†\\mathrm{ln}z: principal branch of logarithm function , cite33†k: nonnegative integer , cite33†m: nonnegative integer and cite33†n: nonnegative integer L151: Keywords:\nL152:     cite75†Stieltjes constants , cite23†definition L153: Sources:\nL154:     Hardy (cite49†1912 , p. 215); Ivić (cite14†1985 , (1.12), p. 4)\nL155: Referenced by:\nL156:     cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite76†§25.6(ii) , cite69†Erratum (V1.0.23) for Subsection 25.2(ii) Other Infinite Series L157: Permalink:\nL158:     cite77†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E5 L159: Encodings:\nL160:     cite78†TeX , cite79†pMML , cite80†png L161: See also:\nL162:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L163: 25.2.6  |  | {\\zeta }^{\\prime }\\left(s\\right)=-\\sum _{n=2}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}(\\mathrm{ln}n){n}^{-s},  |\nL164: \\mathrm{\\Re }s>1.\nL165: ⓘ\nL166: Symbols:\nL167:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite74†\\mathrm{ln}z: principal branch of logarithm function , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L168: Keywords:\nL169:     cite35†infinite series L170: Source:\nL171:     Apostol (cite13†1976 , (12), p. 236)\nL172: Permalink:\nL173:     cite81†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E6 L174: Encodings:\nL175:     cite82†TeX , cite83†pMML , cite84†png L176: See also:\nL177:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L178: 25.2.7  |  | {\\zeta }^{(k)}\\left(s\\right)={(-1)}^{k}\\sum _{n=2}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}{(\\mathrm{ln}n)}^{k}{n}^{-s},  |\nL179: \\mathrm{\\Re }s>1, k=1,2,3,\\mathrm{\\dots }.\nL180: ⓘ\nL181: Symbols:\nL182:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite74†\\mathrm{ln}z: principal branch of logarithm function , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†k: nonnegative integer , cite33†n: nonnegative integer and cite34†s: complex variable L183: Keywords:\nL184:     cite35†infinite series L185: Source:\nL186:     Apostol (cite13†1976 , p. 236); with f(n)=1\nL187: Permalink:\nL188:     cite85†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E7 L189: Encodings:\nL190:     cite86†TeX , cite87†pMML , cite88†png L191: See also:\nL192:     Annotations for cite60†§25.2(ii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L193: For further expansions of functions similar to (cite53†25.2.1 ) (Dirichlet series) see §cite89†27.4 . This includes, for example, 1/\\zeta \\left(s\\right).\nL194: ## §25.2(iii) Representations by the Euler–Maclaurin Formula\nL195: \nL196: ⓘ\nL197: \nL198: Keywords:\nL199:     cite11†Riemann zeta function , cite90†representations by Euler–Maclaurin formula L200: Permalink:\nL201:     cite91†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.iii L202: See also:\nL203:     Annotations for cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 L204: \nL205: 25.2.8  |  | \\zeta \\left(s\\right)=\\sum _{k=1}^{N}\\frac{1}{{k}^{s}}+\\frac{{N}^{1-s}}{s-1}-s{\\int }_{N}^{\\mathrm{\\infty }}\\frac{x-\\lfloor x\\rfloor }{{x}^{s+1}}dx,  |\nL206: \\mathrm{\\Re }s>0, N=1,2,3,\\mathrm{\\dots }.\nL207: ⓘ\nL208: Symbols:\nL209:     cite53†\\zeta \\left(s\\right): Riemann zeta function , cite92†dx: differential of x , cite93†\\lfloor x\\rfloor : floor of x , cite92†\\int : integral , cite54†\\mathrm{\\Re }: real part , cite33†k: nonnegative integer , cite94†x: real variable , cite95†a: real or complex parameter and cite34†s: complex variable L210: Keywords:\nL211:     cite96†Euler–Maclaurin formula , cite97†improper integral L212: Source:\nL213:     Apostol (cite13†1976 , (25), p. 269)\nL214: Proof sketch:\nL215:     Derivable from Apostol (cite13†1976 , Theorem 12.21, p. 269) by setting a=1 and N\\mapsto N-1.\nL216: A&S Ref:\nL217:     23.2.9\nL218: Referenced by:\nL219:     cite98†(25.2.9) L220: Permalink:\nL221:     cite99†http://dlmf.nist.gov/25.2.E8 L222: Encodings:\nL223:     cite100†TeX , cite101†pMML , cite102†png L224: See also:\nL225:     Annotations for cite103†§25.2(iii) , cite32†§25.2 and cite18†Ch.25 "
